desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "File Disclosure"
	title_zh: "File Disclosure"
	type: vuln
	level: high
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-file-disclosure"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `file-disclosure` (ruby/lang/security/file-disclosure.yaml).
Original message: Special requests can determine whether a file exists on a filesystem that's outside the Rails app's root directory. To fix this, set config.serve_static_assets = false.
CWE: CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')
References:
- https://github.com/presidentbeef/brakeman/blob/main/lib/brakeman/checks/check_file_disclosure.rb
- https://groups.google.com/g/rubyonrails-security/c/23fiuwb1NBA/m/MQVM1-5GkPMJ
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Preferred replacement: = false
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.rb": <<<POS
config.serve_static_assets = true
POS
	"safefile://pos.rb": <<<NEG
config.serve_static_assets = false
NEG
)

${*.rb}.pattern_regex(/(?:config\.serve_static_assets\s+=\s+true)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "high",
	title: "File Disclosure",
	title_zh: "File Disclosure",
	message: "File Disclosure detected.",
}
